# Prime review — recorded boot prototype
Date: 2026-10-27. Reviewer: Codex Prime.
Disposition: fixture happy path verified; acceptance HELD pending PB-06 and PB-07.

All16 pinned snapshots and all8 captured outputs match. The dedicated submission
matches0113. Fresh capture verify and inspection complete without changing package
bytes. Independent disposable-copy suite:18 tests pass, no skips. Independent demo
preserves a partial first attempt and an oriented linked second attempt, using
explicit fixture answers and judgement, not an actual model boot. Source review
confirms bounded full-text committed references, distinct live observations,
recorded absence/overflow, fixed tools, external attempt records and no authority
grant. Clerk-job boot and member structured identity remain deferred by this pack.

PB-06 — Wrong-shaped valid JSON escapes validation. With a valid in-scope O1 target,
citations:null raises TypeError after20.answers.raw, leaving no22.checks.json.
A valid judgement envelope with grades.O1={} likewise raises TypeError after
30.judgement.raw, leaving no31 judgement or39 outcome. Raw bytes survive, but the
user receives a traceback rather than a recorded failed stage. These are malformed
data, not simulated process interruptions. Exact CLI outputs/attempts are in probes/.

PB-07 — Identical retries after both crashes return exit0/already-recorded solely
because the raw input file exists. In the first case no check result exists; in the
second no outcome exists. There is no false oriented file, which is good, but a
caller cannot treat this success-shaped replay as evidence the stage completed.
Retries need a recorded terminal state or explicit partial/attention response,
with no rewriting prior bytes or manufacturing completion from supplied grades.

Next bounded repair covers nested shape validation and stage-aware retry reporting
only. Keep valid outcomes, fixed tool pins and authority separation. Do not yet
integrate a live Prime, Clerk or newly accepted inspector. Old temporary fixture
residue reported by the Builder remains untouched; no broad cleanup is authorized.
